---
// GITTACA privacy policy — reachable by direct URL for the Chrome Web Store /
// Firefox AMO listing, but never advertised or indexed (noindex + sitemap
// filter in astro.config.mjs; parity with project `unlisted` pages).
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
import Section from '@/components/Section.astro';
---

<Base
  title="GITTACA — Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for the GITTACA teaching-assistant browser extension."
  noindex
>
  <Section index="§" title="GITTACA Privacy Policy" meta="browser extension">
    <div class="legal" data-pagefind-ignore>
      <p class="legal__lead">
        GITTACA is a browser extension for teaching assistants. It runs entirely in your browser: no
        servers, no analytics, no advertising, no accounts. Your data never reaches the developer of
        this extension.
      </p>

      <h3>Data stored on your device</h3>
      <p>
        Everything the extension keeps lives in the browser's extension storage (<code
          >chrome.storage.local</code
        >) on your own device and never leaves it, except as described under Network requests:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Module on/off toggles and appearance settings.</li>
        <li>Your template packs and remembered template-variable defaults.</li>
        <li>Your per-course semester schedules parsed from syllabi you paste.</li>
        <li>Your Vocareum API token, if you choose to save one (see below).</li>
        <li>
          Optionally cached copies of submissions you grade, if you enable unlimitedStorage for
          submission caching.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Clearing the data from the extension's settings page, or removing the extension, deletes all
        of it.
      </p>

      <h3>Network requests</h3>
      <p>
        The extension makes network requests only to services you already use, from your own
        logged-in session, to perform the action you asked for:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Vocareum</strong> (<code>api.vocareum.com</code>): with the API token you provide,
          the extension downloads the submission files of the students you are grading through
          Vocareum's own API. The token is sent only to Vocareum.
        </li>
        <li>Requests the page itself makes are unaffected.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The extension sends nothing to the developer, has no telemetry, and includes no third-party
        trackers, ads, or analytics of any kind.
      </p>

      <h3>Website content</h3>
      <p>
        When a module is enabled, its content script reads the page it runs on to provide its
        features — for example rendering the submission you are grading on Vocareum, compacting the
        Ed Discussion list, or inserting a template at your cursor in a Slack/Ed/Canvas/Discord
        composer. This content is processed locally in the tab and is not transmitted anywhere by
        the extension.
      </p>

      <h3>Limited Use disclosure</h3>
      <p>
        GITTACA complies with the Chrome Web Store
        <a href="https://developer.chrome.com/docs/webstore/program-policies/user-data-policy"
          >User Data Policy</a
        >, including the Limited Use requirements:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>User data is used only to provide the extension's user-facing features.</li>
        <li>User data is not sold or transferred to third parties.</li>
        <li>User data is not used for advertising, credit checking, or lending.</li>
        <li>
          User data is not used or transferred for purposes unrelated to the extension's single
          purpose.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Authentication data</h3>
      <p>
        The optional Vocareum API token is stored locally, is sent only to Vocareum's own API to
        fetch the submissions you are grading, and is never transmitted anywhere else.
      </p>

      <p class="legal__footer">
        Maintained for internal GT course staff use. Last updated 2026-08-25.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal {
    max-width: 68ch;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }
  .legal__lead {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .legal h3 {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    font-size: var(--step-0);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-mono);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .legal ul {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-1);
    padding-left: var(--space-4);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  .legal code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.9em;
  }
  .legal__footer {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }
</style>
